		<rdf:type rdf:resource="&v;MaxBoundedCompliancePolicy"/>
		<rdfs:label>air movement out to adjacent area (PE room)</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>CDC (2003) Guidelines for Environmental Infection Control in Health-Care
      Facilities, Appendix B, Table B.2, protective environment room: Out. Air movement relationship
      made measurable through the incoming transfer airflow rate (return + exhaust - supply); bound
      is the 125 cfm = 212 m3/h supply/exhaust offset recommended by the AIA (2001) guidelines cited
      in the CDC document.</rdfs:comment>
		<qu:hasUpperBound rdf:resource="https://tw.rpi.edu/ontology-engineering/oe2026/ventilation-compliance/test-individuals/UB_P_PE_AIRMOVE"/>
